[center][size=6][b][color=#e5793a]Idle Life[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4]Somewhere to be, for everyone around you.[/size][/center]

In Fallout 4, people near you mostly just stand around, because there are few places for them to warm their hands, lean or sit. Idle Life gives them more. They warm their hands at fires, have coffee at counters, lean on real walls and sit in a circle round a campfire. The spots are added while the game runs, and are gone when you leave.

[size=5][b][color=#e5793a]In short[/color][/b][/size]

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]People near you use fires, counters, walls, benches, workbenches and more, each kind where it belongs.[/*]
[*]They stay a minute or so, then move on by themselves.[/*]
[*]Enough to feel alive, never a field of props.[/*]
[/list][b]What you need[/b]: F4SE and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url]. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] is optional, for the settings.
[b]How it goes[/b]: install with Vortex or MO2. The installer checks your setup first. See [b]Requirements[/b], below.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-idle-life@a9d2283917db46f8b7f021595c0b22553bbeefd0/docs/img/rule.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Placed the way Bethesda places them.[/b] Measured from the game's own spots: hands warmed 69 units from the fire, campfire sitters 131 out. People stay a minute or so, then move on by themselves.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-idle-life@a9d2283917db46f8b7f021595c0b22553bbeefd0/docs/img/navmesh.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Real walls, no spots over a drop.[/b] Papyrus, the game's scripting language, can't see walls. So a small F4SE plugin reads the ground the game walks on (the navmesh) to find real walls and to keep spots away from drops.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-idle-life@a9d2283917db46f8b7f021595c0b22553bbeefd0/docs/img/budget.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Enough to feel alive, never a field of props.[/b] 1.5 spots per person, 3 to 40, drawn across 18 kinds to fit the place.[/center]

[size=5][b][color=#e5793a]Every kind of spot[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fires and campfires, counters, tables and benches, rails and walls, open ground, boxes and crates, crops.[/*]
[*]Workbenches by type: power armor, chems, tools.[/*]
[*]Radios (dancing), pool tables, TVs, gates.[/*]
[*]Every vanilla pose that fits a place: hands on a rail looking out, bent over a map, rummaging a crate, welding, painting a wall, sweeping, hoeing and weeding, a guard post, push-ups, a prayer, a lookout.[/*]
[*]Robots and dogs: Mr Handy gets some gardening and hedge trimming.[/*]
[*]Spots next to people that suit the place: raiders with Jet and knives, settlers with clipboards and brooms, townsfolk with newspapers and their Pip-Boy. Children sit on the ground.[/*]
[*]At night, fires and radios draw more people.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5][b][color=#e5793a]Settings (MCM)[/color][/b][/size]
Spots per person, the maximum, a daily reshuffle, a switch for each kind, and a Testing page (spawn test settlers, status, a detailed log for bug reports).

[size=5][b][color=#e5793a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]F4SE[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url] (one plugin for every game version)[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional, for the settings)[/*]
[/list]Fallout 4 1.10.163, Next-Gen or the Anniversary Edition. No masters beyond Fallout4.esm; the DLC are used when you have them. Without F4SE or Runtime Database only the spots along walls and in the open are off, and Idle Life says so in game. Install with Vortex or MO2: the installer checks your setup first. Installing by hand is not supported.

IdleLife.dll is [url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/465127378f44a7003b35330a4f931ce295ef0327f23eccf6991f1e85248f632c]clean on VirusTotal[/url] (0/75). Licence: PolyForm Noncommercial.
